en at 31 Leman Street, Goodman’s Fields, distributing 2,550 rations weekly.", "organizer_id": "soup-kitchen-jewish-poor", "place_id": "london", "beneficiary_place_id": "london", "currency": "GBP", "image": "/images/jewish-chronicle-1856-02-15-p481-soup-kitchen.jpg", "image_credit": "Internet Archive (from microfilm)", "iiif_manifest": "", "status": "full transcription — not yet checked", "transcriber": "Claude (draft)", "featured": "no", "notes": "Front-page appeal: donations fell far short of the previous year while distress had increased. A donor of five guineas could nominate one person to a permanent ticket for the season (two portions three times a week). Persons relieved in the week ending 8 February 1856: 2,650; since the start of the season, 17,600; total 20,250. 31 donations totalling £53 1s. as transcribed; no total is printed. Places and addresses are given only where printed; London street addresses are placed in London."}], "roles": [{"list_id": "jewish-soup-kitchen-1856-02-15", "entity_id": "adler-nathan-marcus", "role": "committee", "name_as_printed": "The Rev. Dr. Adler", "address_as_printed": "", "note": "Patron"}, {"list_id": "jewish-soup-kitchen-1856-02-15", "entity_id": "", "role": "committee", "name_as_printed": "The Rt. Hon. the Lord Mayor", "address_as_printed": "", "note": "Patron"}, {"list_id": "jewish-soup-kitchen-1856-02-15", "entity_id": "montefiore-moses", "role": "committee", "name_as_printed": "Sir Moses Montefiore, Bart., F.R.S.", "address_as_printed": "", "note": "Patron"}, {"list_id": "jewish-soup-kitchen-1856-02-15", "entity_id": "", "role": "president", "name_as_printed": "Philip Beyfus, Esq.", "address_as_printed": "", "note": ""}, {"list_id": "jewish-soup-kitchen-1856-02-15", "entity_id": "", "role": "committee", "name_as_printed": "Henry Lyons, Esq.", "address_as_printed": "", "note": "Vice-president"}, {"list_id": "jewish-soup-kitchen-1856-02-15", "entity_id": "", "role": "treasurer", "name_as_printed": "Isaac Hyam, Esq.", "ad